"1. **Previews:** every artifact preview that needs a script has been dead on the web since 26 Aug (D1). The `srcdoc` sandbox inherits the enforcing app CSP, which uses a nonce and `strict-dynamic` (`src/middleware.ts:55-77`, `src/lib/csp.ts:31`). This hits React, scripted HTML, Mermaid, JS/Python, the public share page and Work site previews; it was reproduced in Chromium, and I re-checked the policy and matcher.\n2. **Silent data loss:** editing an earlier message (critical, D2), Regenerate (D3) and deleting a chat (D11) each hard-delete artifacts with their hand edits, design checkpoints, comments and share links. None warns, and native apps branch on edit where the web deletes.\n3. **Model blind to user work:** the model never sees the current artifact, so a plain follow-up overwrites user edits (D5). A chat revision of a design rebuilds it and deletes components, variables, effects, motion and comments (D6). A cut or stopped revision becomes the current version and is labelled \"verified\" (D7).\n4. **Design in conversations:** the inline card shows JSON, the in-chat editor breaks on its first edit (D4, since 5 Aug), and a shared design shows JSON (D10). The chat grammar's `image` node always fails (D9), and the size cap is checked before a 6.5\u00d7 expansion (D8).\n5. **Design engine:** strong, with 37 atomic, invertible operations and 277/277 tests. But the renderer ignores container opacity and rotation (D16), auto-layout fill and grid are wrong, several undos lose data, and exports return 500 on names like \"Tom\u2019s app\" (D15).\n6. **Design editor:** a rich inspector, but Escape commits instead of cancelling (reproduced). There is no drawing or rotate preview, no marquee inside frames, no touch support, and it is unusable below laptop width. Ask Juno is blind, single-turn and non-streaming.\n7. **IA and links:** made things live in four places with inconsistent names. Project pages always show 0 artifacts (D17), the library stops at 200, and Work .docx/.pptx are unreachable on the web (D18). Public links have no moderation, takedown, report link or rate limits, a banned user's pages keep serving, and snapshots leak later edits.\n8. **Scale and observability:** every read ships every version body; an hour of design editing makes a 9\u201327 MB thread payload, and each transaction reads the whole history twice. Nothing is instrumented, and the Mac design editor bundle is stale (`--check` fails).\n9. **Scorecard:** capability 6, UX 3, visual design 6, motion 6, reliability 2, code health 5.\n10. **Merge:** DESIGN is already a typed Artifact, so the merge is a product unification, not a data migration. Order: run previews from a separate origin; give artifacts their own owner, lifetime and soft delete; give the model the current version and one edit protocol; render designs as SVG everywhere; trim payloads; add governance and telemetry; fold Work deliverables in as typed specs.\n\nThe document is at `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-liammagnier-Developer-project-juno/bfdee244-0283-4629-a3f4-3c603fc89908/scratchpad/audit/01-AUDIT-WEB.md`."